# oracle: fix srd with a fix deform that scales the box (x and y scale 1.25, constant rate) and the SRD thermostat (tstat yes, biased streaming bins), 2d (w79srd_deform with tstat yes, 150 steps: the per-atom state is chaotic beyond about 160 steps, see the header measurement)
# Measured max relative error, engine vs native (thermo rows, final atoms): thermo 8.3e-14, atoms 1.2e-9 (chaotic: a native run with the timestep changed by 5e-16 relative drifts the same way, 7.7e-7 at step 200, so the case stops at step 150).
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all
# Measured with native LAMMPS (black box, per-step dumps of the 200-step input): changing the timestep by 5e-16 relative (0.0200000000000001) moves the per-atom state of the run by the same amount of growth as the engine differs from native (7.5e-14 relative at step 20, 7.7e-7 at step 200), so the per-atom state of the SRD thermostat with a deforming box is chaotic: the case stops at step 150, where the per-atom error stays below 1e-8.
units		lj
atom_style	atomic
atom_modify	first empty
dimension	2

lattice		sq 0.4
region		box block 0 3 0 3 -0.5 0.5
create_box	1 box

lattice		sq 0.4
region		plane block 0 3 0 3 -0.001 0.001
lattice		sq 85.0
create_atoms	1 region plane

group		empty type 2

mass		1 0.01
velocity	all create 1.0 593849 loop geom

neighbor	0.3 bin
neigh_modify	delay 1 every 1 check no

comm_modify	group empty

timestep	0.02

fix		1 all srd 1 NULL 1.0 0.25 49894 collision slip tstat yes
fix		2 all enforce2d
fix		3 all deform 1 x scale 1.25 y scale 1.25

thermo_style	custom step temp f_1[7] etotal press f_1[3] f_1[4] f_1[6]
thermo_modify	format float %.15g
thermo		20

run		150
